  <section class="setting setting--tint" data-reveal>
    <div class="court">
      <div class="setting__head"><h2>The questions people actually ask</h2></div>
      <div class="questions">
        <details class="question">
          <summary>What do people wear?</summary>
          <div><p>Anything. You will see suits and you will see shorts, and neither gets a second look.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="question">
          <summary>Thirty-five minutes of preaching?</summary>
          <div><p>Yes, and it is the reason most of the congregation is here. If it is not what you are after, that is a perfectly reasonable conclusion to reach and nobody will chase you about it.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="question">
          <summary>Will I have to talk to anyone?</summary>
          <div><p>Somebody will say hello at the door and then leave you alone. If you want to slip out during the last song, several people do that every week.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="question">
          <summary>What about my children?</summary>
          <div><p>Groups for 3–11s during the sermon, and a creche for under-3s. Everyone working with them is DBS-checked and our safeguarding policy is on the about page. Children are welcome to stay in throughout instead.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="question">
          <summary>Do I have to give money?</summary>
          <div><p>No, and visitors are specifically asked not to. There is a box by the door rather than a collection during the service, which spares everybody the moment.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="question">
          <summary>Is the building accessible?</summary>
          <div><p>Step-free from Chapel Street, an accessible WC, a hearing loop and large-print Bibles. The gallery is up steep stairs and is not accessible.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

